  "restrictedArea": {
    "id": "AREA_OF_ARTICULATION",
    "fromFrame": "39.2",
    "toFrame": "40",
    "rules": [
      "Long items with a high stiffness (high moment of resistance) shall not be loaded across the area.",
      "Use of floating pallets is not allowed in the area."
    ]
  },
  "exclusivity": {
    "rule": "FOOTPRINT_OVERLAP",
    "note": "Two positions conflict when their longitudinal footprints overlap and their lateral placements are not disjoint. The footprint is centred on the position's arm, which is derived from positions.json indexPerKg (arm = refSta + C x indexPerKg), and is longitudinalInches long. This plate prints alternative row configurations of one physical floor; it does not print a conflict matrix, so the matrix is computed, never transcribed.",
    "verifiedExamples": [
      "Lower deck: {12P,13P} tile exactly the floor of containers {12,13,14} (16.438 m - 21.123 m); likewise {21P,22P} over {21,22,23}, {31P,32P} over {31,32,33} and {41P,42P} over {41,42,43}. That is why 11P and 43P do not exist - container 11 has no pallet equivalent.",
      "Main deck: the SINGLE ROW 88\" x 125\" position X occupies exactly loading zone X of loading-zones-harm.json, to within the rounding of indexPerKg."
    ]
  },
  "notes": [
    "Row titles read <fore-aft>\" x <lateral>\": SINGLE ROW 88\" x 125\" is 88 in of deck pitch and 125 in across. Confirmed three ways - the 88 in pitch matches loading-zones-harm.json, the 125 in side-by-side rows share their arm with the SINGLE ROW 125\" x 96\" bridge position of the same name, and the lateral imbalance y-arms are half the lateral width (1.13 m for 88 in, 1.23 m for 96 in).",
    "Max loads are transcribed from the approved plate and independently confirmed against the operator's laminated LOAD AND TRIM SHEET card photographed on 2026-09-09; the two agree cell for cell.",
    "The lower-deck row is titled 60.4\" x 61.5\" OR 60.4\" x 125\": each numbered position takes either one full-size unit at 3174 kg or two half-size units (L and R) at 1587 kg each. The LIR prints the half-size variants as 11R/11L .. 43R/43L.",
    "SIDE BY SIDE 125\" x 88\" carries a tenth pair (PRR/PRL) that SIDE BY SIDE 125\" x 96\" does not.",
    "Both side-by-side rows print identical max loads pair for pair; only the longitudinal pitch differs.",
    "The 16 ft and 20 ft pallet rows also carry printed zone distribution factors; those live in zone-mapping.json.",
    "The 16 ft and 20 ft pallet rows are not printed on the approved plate's page 2; they come from the operator's laminated card only, and their max loads are corroborated by positions.json rather than by a second printing of the plate."
  ],
  "source": {
    "documentTitle": "AHM 560 - Airbus A330-243 P2F - Appendix I, LOAD AND TRIM SHEET page 2 (printed p.74), Ed.1 Rev.0, effective 15.03.2023",
